    "chunk_size_bytes": 1833,
    "chunk_text": "In relation to the case No. DSP 99/2018 filed by private film distribution circuits against National Film Corporation,the order of suspension, which has been issued by Court suspending the notification made by the Chairman of NationalFilm Corporation of Sri Lanka to film distribution circuits on 19.06.2018 making the agreement/understanding which hasbeen made between Corporation and distribution circuits entrusting film distribution to private circuits, null and void, hasbeen dissolved and further interim injunction requested from the Court against National Film Corporation by privatedistribution circuits has also been rejected.\n\nANUSHA GOKULA FERNANDO,Chairperson,The National Film Corporation of Sri Lanka.18th June, 2019.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'07'03PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA 03.07.20192A\n\n28th June 2019.NFC/100/01/020(III)\n\nAll Film Producers,Theatre Owners/Lessees/Managers,Film Importers\n\nMethodology for distribution and screening of filmsNational Film Corporation of Sri Lanka\n\n1. Introduction\n\nBy virtue of the powers vested in the Chairman under Section 57 of National Film Corporation of Sri Lanka Act No 47 of1971 amended by Act No 45 of 1980, powers which have been entertained so far by private distribution circuits, have beencancelled from 18 June 2019 and from that date National Film Corporation of Sri Lanka performs all the functionsincluding scheduling films for cinema halls, releasing films for screening and collecting income from the distribution offilms totally as per the powers of the aforesaid acts.\n\n2. Methodology\n\nDistribution of films within Sri Lanka shall be performed by National Film Corporation of Sri Lanka (Hereinafter referredto as \u201cCorporation\u201d)."
  },
